{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"LoomCore uses Swift’s string interpolation as its primary SQL-construction API. Every interpolated value defaults to ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".bind"},{"type":"text","text":" mode"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — it is added to the statement as a parameter (","type":"text"},{"code":"?","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") and its value is bound at execution time. This is the safe path; you cannot accidentally concatenate user input into the SQL text.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let user = \"Alice'; DROP TABLE users; --\"","try await db.exec(\"INSERT INTO users (name) VALUES (\\(user))\")","\/\/ SQL: \"INSERT INTO users (name) VALUES (?)\"","\/\/ Bound: \"Alice'; DROP TABLE users; --\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The malicious payload becomes a literal string value in the database. There is no way to break out of the parameter binding.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Raw-mode","text":"Raw mode"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Some things cannot be parameters — table names, column names, SQL keywords. For these, opt in to ","type":"text"},{"code":".raw","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" mode:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let table = \"users\"  \/\/ from your own configuration, NOT user input","try await db.exec(\"SELECT * FROM \\(table, mode: .raw) WHERE active = \\(true)\")","\/\/ SQL: \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE active = ?\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":".raw","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" skips parameter binding and pastes the value directly into the SQL string. This is exactly the surface SQL injection lives on.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"warning","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Never pass untrusted input through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".raw"},{"type":"text","text":". If user input determines a table or column name, validate it against an allowlist of known names before using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".raw"},{"type":"text","text":", or use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/ColumnExpression"},{"type":"text","text":" which always quotes identifiers safely."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Warning"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"ColumnExpression-the-safe-identifier-path","text":"ColumnExpression — the safe identifier path"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When you need to refer to a column by name, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/ColumnExpression","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is preferable to ","type":"text"},{"code":".raw","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let nameColumn = ColumnExpression<String>(\"name\")","let userEmail  = ColumnExpression<String>(\"email\", of: \"users\")","","try await db.query(\"SELECT \\(nameColumn) FROM users\") { stmt, _ in","  try String.column(of: stmt, at: 0)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ColumnExpression","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" always renders quoted identifiers (","type":"text"},{"code":"\"name\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"users\".\"email\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), escapes embedded double quotes by doubling, and rejects empty or NUL-containing names at construction. This makes reserved words like ","type":"text"},{"code":"order","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and identifiers with spaces safe to use without special handling.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"JSON-paths-literal-by-design","text":"JSON paths — literal by design"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONPath","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" values (the ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"$.name\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" arguments of the JSON expressions) render as single-quoted, quote-doubled literals rather than bound parameters — the same treatment as ","type":"text"},{"code":"LIKE","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"ESCAPE","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" operand. SQLite matches an expression index on ","type":"text"},{"code":"json_extract(\"col\", '$.a')","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" only when the path is a literal token, so binding it would silently disable indexed JSON lookups. The doubling makes breaking out of the literal impossible, but a path still selects which node is read — treat it like a column name, not user input.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Composing-statements","text":"Composing statements"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SQLStatement","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" values can be combined while preserving parameter ordering:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let minAge = 18","","var stmt: SQLStatement = \"SELECT * FROM users\"","stmt += \"WHERE age > \\(minAge)\"","stmt += \"ORDER BY name\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each fragment carries its own binders; concatenation appends them in order. There is no parameter-renumbering to worry about.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"article","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/loomcore\/safeinterpolation"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"When "},{"code":"\\(value)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" becomes a parameter, when it becomes literal text, and how to keep injection-prone surfaces small."}],"metadata":{"role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Safe SQL Interpolation","modules":[{"name":"LoomCore"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SafeInterpolation","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SQLStatement","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SQLBuilder","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SQLBuilder\/AppendMode","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/ColumnExpression"],"anchor":"Topics"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/IndexConventions","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/ConcurrencyModel","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/StoringCustomTypes","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/QueryingJSON","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FullTextSearch","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionsAndServices"],"title":"Articles","anchor":"Articles","generated":true}],"references":{"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/FullTextSearch":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Match, rank, and excerpt text with typed expressions over SQLite’s FTS5 extension."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FullTextSearch","title":"Full-Text Search","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/fulltextsearch"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/IndexConventions":{"abstract":[{"text":"How LoomCore handles SQLite’s asymmetric 1-based parameter \/ 0-based column indexing.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/IndexConventions","title":"Index Conventions","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/indexconventions"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/QueryingJSON":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extract, filter, modify, build, and iterate JSON documents with typed expressions over SQLite’s JSON functions."}],"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/queryingjson","title":"Querying JSON","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/QueryingJSON","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/TransactionsAndServices":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionsAndServices","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Transactions and Services","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/transactionsandservices","abstract":[{"text":"Atomic operations, savepoint nesting, transaction gating, and lifecycle hooks for cache invalidation.","type":"text"}]},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/ColumnExpression":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"ColumnExpression","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Typed reference to a SQL column, optionally qualified by a table name.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/ColumnExpression","url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/columnexpression","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ColumnExpression"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ColumnExpression","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type-safe SQLite wrapper for Swift 6+ built on actor isolation."}],"title":"LoomCore","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore","type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/loomcore"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/StoringCustomTypes":{"abstract":[{"text":"How ","type":"text"},{"code":"Bindable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" maps Swift types to SQLite storage, and how to extend it.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/StoringCustomTypes","title":"Storing Custom Types","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/storingcustomtypes"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/SQLStatement":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SQLStatement"}],"title":"SQLStatement","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SQLStatement"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"SQL statement with safe parameter binding."}],"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/sqlstatement","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SQLStatement","kind":"symbol"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/JSONPath":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"JSONPath"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A SQLite JSON path such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"$.user.name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$[0]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"code":"$.\"key with spaces\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"JSONPath"}],"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/jsonpath","title":"JSONPath","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONPath","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/SQLBuilder":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"SQLBuilder","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"String interpolation handler that builds "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SQLStatement","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" values with safe parameter binding."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SQLBuilder","url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/sqlbuilder","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SQLBuilder"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SQLBuilder"}]},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/SQLBuilder/AppendMode":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AppendMode","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/sqlbuilder\/appendmode","abstract":[{"text":"Controls how an interpolated value is rendered into the SQL.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AppendMode","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SQLBuilder\/AppendMode","kind":"symbol","title":"SQLBuilder.AppendMode","role":"symbol"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/ConcurrencyModel":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How LoomCore makes SQLite race-free without explicit locking."}],"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/concurrencymodel","title":"Concurrency and Actor Isolation","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/ConcurrencyModel","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup"}}}